          "p": "The single idea which, once genuinely taken in, changes how a person lives the next day: the dichotomy of control. Everything else in Stoicism (the cosmic stuff, the talk of the *logos*, the rehearsals of death) is in service to this one move, and Marcus returns to it more than to anything else. It did not start with Marcus. He inherited it, whole, from Epictetus, whose handbook opens with it. Epictetus's statement of it is the thing Marcus is forever applying."
