          "p": "The dichotomy of control is the engine. Marcus runs it by means of two great exercises, two mental tricks he plays on himself, over and over, to make the principle actually feel true rather than merely known. The difficulty with the dichotomy of control is that knowing intellectually that one's reputation isn't up to oneself does very little when that reputation is being torn apart and the stomach is in knots. The principle needs support to bite. Marcus's two main forms of support are a zoom-out in space and a zoom-out in time: roughly, the view from above, and the steady rehearsal of death."
